# text = Mysticism , with its marvellous power of making common things strange to us , and the subtle antinomianism that always seems to accompany it , moved him for a season ; and for a season he inclined to the materialistic doctrines of the Darwinismus movement in Germany , and found a curious pleasure in tracing the thoughts and passions of men to some pearly cell in the brain , or some white nerve in the body , delighting in the conception of the absolute dependence of the spirit on certain physical conditions , morbid or healthy , normal or diseased .
