# text = As he rode home , his eyes were full of tears , for he knew he was safe cried Lord Henry , dipping his white fingers into a red copper bowl filled with rose-water Dorian Gray shook his head said Lord Henry , smiling echoed Dorian asked his companion as he spilled into his plate a little crimson pyramid of seeded strawberries and , through a perforated , shell-shaped spoon , snowed white sugar upon them interrupted Lord Henry said Lord Henry , laughing , as he leaned back in his chair said Dorian , pouring himself out some wine and frowning slightly asked Dorian , holding up his Burgundy against the light and wondering how it was that he could discuss the matter so calmly said the younger man wearily said Lord Henry , passing beneath his nostrils the gilt trellis of an open vinaigrette box Dorian said nothing , but rose from the table , and passing into the next room , sat down to the piano and let his fingers stray across the white and black ivory of the keys .
